data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793768059781, "messageId": "a15d945e5d", "delta": "I recommend **2 doublets at 2,500 m, heat pump top-up and a gas boiler (3 units), absorption and electric chillers, two injectors on doublet 1, a treatment train (separator, filters) per doublet, sized so that any one unit can be out (N-1): boiler and chillers in equal units** (A1 · 2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-N1-FC), the best overall: a reliable plan (any one unit can be out and every day is still met) and, of those, the cheapest when CO₂ counts at 137 €/t (the long-term price). It meets heat at 100 °C and cold at 20 °C every day of 2027 for 72.8 €/MWh of heat and cold together (heat 81.9 €/MWh, cold 30.1 €/MWh), with 64% less CO₂ than gas boilers and electric chillers, and passes all 16 checks. Its heat: the geothermal exchanger 51.6%, the heat pump 22.3%, the gas boiler 26.1% (it burns the produced gas first and buys 14.4 GWh of gas a year)."}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END", "timestamp": 1793768059781, "messageId": "a15d945e5d"}

