data: {"type": "RUN_FINISHED", "timestamp": 1793768059792, "threadId": "fixture-build", "runId": "936985e68b", "outcome": {"type": "success"}, "usage": [{"model": "scripted", "provider": "ollama", "inputTokens": 300, "outputTokens": 60, "totalTokens": 360}], "result": {"behaviour": "design", "asked": [], "answer": "I recommend **2 doublets at 2,500 m, heat pump top-up and a gas boiler (3 units), absorption and electric chillers, two injectors on doublet 1, a treatment train (separator, filters) per doublet, sized so that any one unit can be out (N-1): boiler and chillers in equal units** (A1 · 2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-N1-FC), the best overall: a reliable plan (any one unit can be out and every day is still met) and, of those, the cheapest when CO₂ counts at 137 €/t (the long-term price). It meets heat at 100 °C and cold at 20 °C every day of 2027 for 72.8 €/MWh of heat and cold together (heat 81.9 €/MWh, cold 30.1 €/MWh), with 64% less CO₂ than gas boilers and electric chillers, and passes all 16 checks. Its heat: the geothermal exchanger 51.6%, the heat pump 22.3%, the gas boiler 26.1% (it burns the produced gas first and buys 14.4 GWh of gas a year).", "ungrounded": [], "dropped": [], "verified": true, "reasoning": false, "reasoning_auto": true, "device": null, "decided_by": {"think": "model", "answer": "model"}, "message": "Design two doublets: the first with two injectors, the second with its own separator and filters.", "intent": "design", "language": "en", "screened": false, "parameters": {"changes": {}, "doublets": 2, "unsupported": [], "dropped": [], "failures": [], "designs": [], "steps": ["design"]}, "plan": ["2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST", "2D-BO-AB-2I1-ST", "2D-BO-EC-2I1-ST", "2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-BL", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST-BL", "2D-BO-AB-2I1-ST-BL", "2D-BO-EC-2I1-ST-BL", "2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-N1", "2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-N1", "2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-BL-N1", "2D-HP-AB-2I1-ST-BL-N1", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST-N1", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST-N1", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST-BL-N1", "2D-HP-EC-2I1-ST-BL-N1", "2D-BO-AB-